  pm-ye46ns,related,"2026-08-07T11:19:54.209Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
body: "## What was measured\n\nMeasured 2026-08-07 against the live workspace: 2,357 items, 9,462 explicit dependency rows, plus parent-field edges.\n\nTraversal rule: follow only typed edges — parent, child, implements, verifies, supersedes, discovered_from, incident_from, blocked_by, blocks. The `related` and `related_to` kinds are excluded because they carry no direction and no semantics, which is precisely why the ontology exists.\n\nQuestion asked: from each item, how many typed hops reach one of the six outcome milestones?\n\n| population | 1 hop | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | never |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| active (350) | 131 | 151 | 59 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 2 |\n| terminal (2,007) | 68 | 785 | 123 | 4 | 1 | 1 | **1,025** |\n\n1,024 of those 1,025 do reach `pm-doxj`, the roadmap apex. Exactly one item reaches nothing at all.\n\n## The topology defect\n\nThe six outcome milestones are **siblings** of the capability epics under the apex, not a layer between them and it. Every outcome milestone carries `implements -> pm-doxj`. Every capability epic carries `parent: pm-doxj` **and** `implements -> <outcome milestone>`. Both are one hop. A shortest-path traversal is therefore free to leave the ladder unvisited, and for half the corpus there is no ladder edge on any path at all.\n\nThe historical record attaches to the apex through 154 typed roots that carry no outcome edge of any kind: 77 closed or canceled Epics (the seven `Milestone 0..6` delivery epics, their seven canceled `PRD Milestone` twins, and the dogfood and external-audit epics such as the 2026-04-30, 2026-05-02, and 2026-05-03 audit programmes), plus Chores, Plans, Tasks, Issues and Features parented straight at the apex. The largest single root carries 415 descendants; ten roots carry more than 200 each.\n\n## Why this is not the items already filed\n\n- The strategic reachability invariant states its terminal clause as resolving *to the index root*. Under that wording all 1,024 items pass today, because the index root is exactly what they reach. The invariant as written cannot detect this.\n- The historical-programme-spine item covers the duplicated v1 milestone encoding — fourteen of the 154 roots. It does not cover the other 140.\n- The graph completeness audit scoping defect is about which nodes are *measured*. This is about which nodes are *reachable through the ladder*, and it is invisible even when every node is measured.\n- The flat-ordering-graph item concerns the ordering kinds. This concerns the hierarchy and implementation kinds.\n\n## Consequence\n\nEvery question of the form \"which outcome does this work serve\", asked of the project's own delivery history, has no typed answer. Critical path, dominators, and blast radius all describe the forward 350 items and treat the 1,993 items that actually built the product as an undifferentiated fan hanging off one node. An agent reconstructing why the product is shaped the way it is cannot walk from an outcome to the work that produced it.\n\n## Boundary\n\nNo edge may be invented to satisfy a count. Historical programmes did not implement forward gates and must not be given `implements` edges to them. The honest relation between the v1 delivery epoch and the post-v0.1 roadmap is succession, and the honest relation between an audit programme and the capability it hardened is evidence. Both are recoverable from durable text already on the items. A root for which no durable evidence exists belongs on a recorded residual list with its reason, not on a fabricated edge."
